# Editing a .tsv in Excel or another GUI tool round-trips it through CRLF line
# endings, and Excel additionally quotes any row whose first cell begins with a
# character it wants to escape, then pads every row out to the full column count
# with empty tabs. That has happened twice to assets/measurements.tsv and both
# times it broke the TSV parsers that read it.
#
# Forcing LF in the working tree means git normalises the file on checkout, so a
# GUI round-trip produces a diff in the values that changed and nothing else.
# It does not stop the quoting or the padding, which is why
# bin/check_measurements.py tolerates both on read.
*.tsv text eol=lf
*.csv text eol=lf
*.py  text eol=lf
*.sh  text eol=lf
*.md  text eol=lf
*.nf  text eol=lf
